course: dictionary
lesson: 11267
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word wren can name a small bird, and it can also be a family name. The context tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: «The tiny wren has one of the loudest songs for its size, which carries through thick bushes.» Here wren is a bird. It is tiny, it sings, and it is in the bushes. A person's name would not sing in a bush.
explain: «In Hull, Wren snores, Tilda throws a pillow, Wren throws a slipper.» Here Wren is a name. The capital letter in the middle of the sentence is a clue, and the snoring and throwing things are things a person does. Ask yourself: does this fit a bird, or a person?
fact: A wren is a tiny brown bird with a short tail that sticks up.
fact: A wren has a very loud song for its size.
fact: Wren is also a family name, as in Sir Christopher Wren.
fact: Sir Christopher Wren was the architect of St Paul's Cathedral in London.
fact: When a word has two meanings, read the sentence to find which one fits.
exercise: «The wren hopped along the hedge, looking for insects.» What is a wren in this sentence? | A family name | *A tiny brown bird | A kind of bridge over a river | A large grey cloud
exercise: «In Hull, Wren snores, and Tilda throws a pillow.» What is Wren in this sentence? | A loud song | A kind of pillow | A tiny bird | *A person's name
exercise: Which fact is about Sir Christopher Wren? | He had a short tail that sticks up | *He was the architect of St Paul's Cathedral in London | He hopped in hedges looking for insects | He had a very loud song for its size
test: «A wren has a very loud song for its size.» What does wren mean here? | A famous church in London | A tall, thin tree | A family name | *A tiny brown bird
test: «Sir Christopher Wren rebuilt many churches in London.» Who is Wren in this sentence? | A friend who snores | A kind of song | *A man, a famous architect | A bird with a short tail
exam: Ella asks, «Is wren always a bird?» What is the answer? | No, it is a kind of song | Yes, it is always a bird | *No, it can also be a family name, so check the context | Yes, it is always a person's name
